  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal word commonly used in business, finance, and government contexts. It implies making up for something that is missing or deficient. The kanji {填|てん} means to fill in.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {赤字|あかじ}{補填|ほてん} (deficit coverage)\n- {損失|そんしつ}{補填|ほてん} (loss compensation)\n- {財源|ざいげん}の{補填|ほてん} (filling a funding gap)\n- {人員|じんいん}の{補填|ほてん} (filling a personnel shortage)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {補充|ほじゅう}: replenishment — restocking or adding more of something\n- {補償|ほしょう}: compensation — making amends for damage or injury",
